1
00:00:55,935 --> 00:00:59,556
Why do they always put braces on teenage girls
at the exact moment when they're most

2
00:00:59,556 --> 00:01:02,385
self-conscious about their appearance?

3
00:01:03,617 --> 00:01:05,055
I don't know

4
00:01:07,455 --> 00:01:08,418
Tom

5
00:01:08,418 --> 00:01:09,377
I see him

6
00:01:09,377 --> 00:01:13,217
Tom! Jesus!

7
00:01:13,217 --> 00:01:17,047
Tom!

8
00:01:32,419 --> 00:01:34,338
Hello, Amy

9
00:01:34,338 --> 00:01:37,219
Hi, Darryl

10
00:01:37,219 --> 00:01:41,048
Amy, would you tell the kids you'll be right back

11
00:01:42,019 --> 00:01:43,939
And, shut the door and step outside...

12
00:01:43,939 --> 00:01:45,859
talk to us for a minute

13
00:01:45,859 --> 00:01:47,779
Okay

14
00:01:47,779 --> 00:01:50,659
Be right back, you guys!

15
00:01:50,659 --> 00:01:51,620
You're not supposed to go out, Amy

16
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:55,449
She's going to smoke a cigarette

17
00:04:33,868 --> 00:04:37,698
Rudy, come on, I'm really late! Come on

18
00:04:47,309 --> 00:04:48,268
How was school?

19
00:04:48,268 --> 00:04:49,228
Stupid

20
00:04:49,228 --> 00:04:51,149
Why do you say that?

21
00:04:51,149 --> 00:04:53,068
We're supposed to write a story
for English homework. But they didn't tell us

22
00:04:53,068 --> 00:04:55,949
what it's supposed to be about

23
00:04:55,949 --> 00:04:57,869
What do you mean?

24
00:04:57,869 --> 00:04:59,791
I mean, they didn't tell us what it's supposed

25
00:04:59,791 --> 00:05:01,710
to be about. They said do whatever you want

26
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:04,590
Well, what's wrong with that?

27
00:05:04,590 --> 00:05:08,430
I don't know, I just think it's unstructured

28
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:11,311
Well I'm sure you'll think of something

29
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:15,139
If you can't, I'll help you

30
00:05:21,872 --> 00:05:25,710
Okay, here... Don't forget your backpack

31
00:05:25,710 --> 00:05:26,672
It's not a backpack, it's a knapsack

32
00:05:26,672 --> 00:05:30,727
Then don't forget the knapsack
Hey, Give me a hug. Okay

33
00:06:18,514 --> 00:06:20,434
Guess who's been asking for you?

34
00:06:20,434 --> 00:06:23,315
Oh no, really? Is that his car?

35
00:06:23,315 --> 00:06:27,156
Oh yeah

36
00:06:27,156 --> 00:06:29,075
Yeah, come in

37
00:06:29,075 --> 00:06:30,034
Mister Everett

38
00:06:30,034 --> 00:06:31,956
Oh yeah, Brian

39
00:06:31,956 --> 00:06:34,834
Brian, hi. I'm Samantha Ann Prescott

40
00:06:34,834 --> 00:06:35,796
I'm the lending officer

41
00:06:35,796 --> 00:06:39,634
Yeah, hi. Hi. How are you. Have a seat

42
00:06:39,634 --> 00:06:41,556
I am so sorry I was late

43
00:06:41,556 --> 00:06:42,517
Yeah, we missed you before...

44
00:06:42,517 --> 00:06:44,434
I got held up...

45
00:06:44,434 --> 00:06:47,317
Believe me, it's nothing I make a habit of

46
00:06:47,317 --> 00:06:49,234
I'm sure it's not

47
00:06:49,234 --> 00:06:53,066
Actually, would you get that door for me, please

48
00:06:54,996 --> 00:06:56,917
So I always run out at 3:15 to meet him...

49
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,797
then run real quick over to the sitters house

50
00:06:59,797 --> 00:07:01,717
Anyway, Larry never seemed
to mind about it, so I was...

51
00:07:01,717 --> 00:07:05,558
just hoping you'd feel the same way about it too

52
00:07:05,558 --> 00:07:09,397
Well, Samantha, I realize that Scotsville...

53
00:07:09,397 --> 00:07:11,318
is not exactly a major banking center

54
00:07:11,318 --> 00:07:12,277
No, it's not

55
00:07:12,277 --> 00:07:14,198
No, I know it's not

56
00:07:14,198 --> 00:07:16,117
But it's kind of a personal challenge to me to see

57
00:07:16,117 --> 00:07:20,916
what we can do to bring local service up to
the kinds of standards that we'd try to meet

58
00:07:20,917 --> 00:07:23,799
if we were the biggest branch in the state

59
00:07:23,799 --> 00:07:29,429
Now, that means I don't want anybody
running out at 3:15 or 3:30 or whenever

60
00:07:29,559 --> 00:07:32,437
the bus happens to come in that day

61
00:07:32,437 --> 00:07:35,318
So is there anybody else who can
pick up your son after school?

62
00:07:35,318 --> 00:07:37,237
Does your husband work in the area?

63
00:07:37,237 --> 00:07:41,079
Ahh, no. Rudy Sr. Isn't on the scene
so to speak

64
00:07:41,079 --> 00:07:44,919
Well, I can give you a few days
to make some other arrangements. But...

65
00:07:44,919 --> 00:07:46,838
Well, Brian...

66
00:07:46,838 --> 00:07:49,720
I understand what you're saying
and I think it's great. I do

67
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:52,601
Because there's a lot of things around here
that could use some attention. Believe me

68
00:07:52,601 --> 00:07:56,440
But I've been meeting this bus
every day for 3 years now

69
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:59,321
And it really does, it takes 15 minutes

70
00:07:59,321 --> 00:08:01,241
And if I take the time out of my lunch hour...

71
00:08:01,241 --> 00:08:05,080
Well, I'd prefer if you would
make some other arrangements, Okay?

72
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:08,920
I'll do my best

73
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:11,801
So, how old's your son?

74
00:08:11,801 --> 00:08:13,721
He's eight

75
00:08:13,721 --> 00:08:17,550
That's a terrific age

76
00:08:59,804 --> 00:09:02,683
You got a letter from Uncle Terry

77
00:09:02,683 --> 00:09:06,514
What?

78
00:09:31,485 --> 00:09:34,366
What room is he going to stay in?

79
00:09:34,366 --> 00:09:38,195
He can stay in the little room

80
00:09:40,126 --> 00:09:42,046
You know what, he's not going to live here

81
00:09:42,046 --> 00:09:45,875
He's only coming here, to stay for a little while

82
00:09:47,806 --> 00:09:50,687
And it's okay if you don't remember
him because

83
00:09:50,687 --> 00:09:53,566
you were only six the last time he was here

84
00:09:53,566 --> 00:09:58,396
But I think it'll be nice
if you got a chance to know each other

85
00:10:00,288 --> 00:10:04,117
Don't you think?

86
00:10:06,048 --> 00:10:08,927
Rudy, would it distract you
if I put on some music?

87
00:10:08,927 --> 00:10:12,759
No

88
00:10:15,648 --> 00:10:17,568
Did you think of a story?

89
00:10:17,568 --> 00:10:20,448
Uh-huh

90
00:10:20,448 --> 00:10:21,407
What's it about?

91
00:10:21,407 --> 00:10:25,238
My father

92
00:10:27,169 --> 00:10:29,089
What... What about your father?

93
00:10:29,089 --> 00:10:32,929
It's just a made-up story about him

94
00:10:32,929 --> 00:10:34,848
Can I read it when you're done?

95
00:10:34,848 --> 00:10:37,730
It's not very good

96
00:10:37,730 --> 00:10:41,559
Don't say that

97
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:22,852
Anyway, Bob, it's kind of this adventure story

98
00:11:22,852 --> 00:11:25,732
Rudy's father is a secret agent...

99
00:11:25,732 --> 00:11:28,612
or something, working for the government

100
00:11:28,612 --> 00:11:31,492
And it made me feel kinda weird. Because

101
00:11:31,492 --> 00:11:34,373
I've never said much to him about Rudy Sr

102
00:11:34,373 --> 00:11:35,332
Because I don't know what to say

103
00:11:35,332 --> 00:11:37,254
And I don't know if I should just let him...

104
00:11:37,254 --> 00:11:41,081
imagine what he wants to imagine

105
00:11:43,014 --> 00:11:45,892
Of if I should sit him down sometime
and you know, tell him...

106
00:11:45,892 --> 00:11:48,773
that his father's not such a nice person

107
00:11:48,773 --> 00:11:51,654
Well I don't know, Sammy
what have you told him already

108
00:11:51,654 --> 00:11:54,533
Not much. He knows...

109
00:11:54,533 --> 00:11:58,364
He knows I don't have the highest opinion
of him

110
00:11:59,333 --> 00:12:02,215
He knows I don't want to see him

111
00:12:02,215 --> 00:12:04,133
That I don't want to know anything about him

112
00:12:04,133 --> 00:12:07,014
Or to have anything to do with him

113
00:12:07,014 --> 00:12:10,845
But I've tired to keep it kinda neutral

114
00:12:13,736 --> 00:12:16,614
Well anyway, I could go
into a lot more detail, believe me

115
00:12:16,614 --> 00:12:20,456
It's an interesting problem
I don't really know what to tell you

116
00:12:20,456 --> 00:12:24,286
It's a little outside my personal field of expertise

117
00:12:25,256 --> 00:12:27,175
Alright

118
00:12:27,175 --> 00:12:29,097
I'd be glad to give it some thought

119
00:12:29,097 --> 00:12:32,924
Okay

120
00:12:37,737 --> 00:12:39,655
What?

121
00:12:39,655 --> 00:12:41,577
No, nothing, I'm just glad to see you

122
00:12:41,577 --> 00:12:44,456
I'm glad you called me

123
00:12:44,456 --> 00:12:46,377
I bet you were surprised

124
00:12:46,377 --> 00:12:50,206
Yeah, a little

125
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:06,539
I should get going

126
00:13:06,539 --> 00:13:07,498
Really?

127
00:13:07,498 --> 00:13:10,378
Yeah, I've got the babysitter

128
00:13:10,378 --> 00:13:14,207
But, thanks for a lovely evening

129
00:13:15,178 --> 00:13:19,007
Oh, thank you

130
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:47,820
Hey

131
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,741
Hey, Terry

132
00:13:49,741 --> 00:13:50,701
Where'd you get that hat?

133
00:13:50,701 --> 00:13:52,620
Got it on the street for a dollar

134
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:55,501
It's nice

135
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:58,381
Well it's pretty much your standard woolen hat

136
00:13:58,381 --> 00:14:02,211
I had a very similar reaction to it

137
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:10,851
Umm... Umm...
Can I get that money from you?

138
00:14:13,743 --> 00:14:17,572
Yeah, sorry

139
00:14:23,343 --> 00:14:25,263
That all you have?

140
00:14:25,263 --> 00:14:29,092
Yeah

141
00:14:30,062 --> 00:14:32,944
Can you borrow some more from your brother?

142
00:14:32,944 --> 00:14:34,862
That would involve speaking to him

143
00:14:34,862 --> 00:14:37,744
Well I'm definitely gonna be gone
for a couple of days, Sheila

144
00:14:37,744 --> 00:14:39,662
Why do you have to stay for so long?

145
00:14:39,662 --> 00:14:40,623
Because my sister's not a bank, okay?

146
00:14:40,623 --> 00:14:41,583
I can't just show up...

147
00:14:41,583 --> 00:14:42,544
You think my brother's a bank!

148
00:14:42,544 --> 00:14:46,383
Can we just cut the puerile crap!

149
00:14:46,383 --> 00:14:47,344
I'll be back as soon as I can, okay!

150
00:14:47,344 --> 00:14:51,185
I'm not the kind of guy everyone says I am

151
00:14:51,185 --> 00:14:55,013
I know you're not

152
00:15:06,546 --> 00:15:10,374
Okay, ahh... I'll call you tonight

153
00:15:19,026 --> 00:15:20,946
Don't you want to tell me that you love me?

154
00:15:20,946 --> 00:15:22,866
I love you

155
00:15:22,866 --> 00:15:26,706
That was really convincing

156
00:15:26,706 --> 00:15:29,586
Well, after this is over I think you should

157
00:15:29,586 --> 00:15:32,467
seriously consider moving back home

158
00:15:32,467 --> 00:15:36,295
Yeah

159
00:15:38,227 --> 00:15:40,146
Alright

160
00:15:40,146 --> 00:15:42,068
So you gonna call me tonight?

161
00:15:42,068 --> 00:15:45,895
Definitely

162
00:17:21,914 --> 00:17:25,744
Hello? Terry!

163
00:17:58,396 --> 00:17:59,355
Whoa... Terry...

164
00:17:59,355 --> 00:18:00,315
That's me

165
00:18:00,315 --> 00:18:01,275
How's it going?

166
00:18:01,275 --> 00:18:02,235
Going good...

167
00:18:02,235 --> 00:18:06,075
Give me a hug
How you doing, good to see you

168
00:18:06,075 --> 00:18:07,036
You too

169
00:18:07,036 --> 00:18:07,996
Where you been?

170
00:18:07,996 --> 00:18:08,957
Man I've been all over the place

171
00:18:08,957 --> 00:18:09,916
Where you headed?

172
00:18:09,916 --> 00:18:10,875
Just going up to see Sammy

173
00:18:10,875 --> 00:18:14,706
Yeah, yeah. So she said you've been to Alaska?

174
00:18:15,676 --> 00:18:19,517
Oh hi, how you going Mr. Parker
Good to see you again. Take care

175
00:18:19,517 --> 00:18:20,476
So you working?

176
00:18:20,476 --> 00:18:22,397
Yeah, yeah

177
00:18:22,397 --> 00:18:24,317
Got a postcard every once in a while

178
00:18:24,317 --> 00:18:27,197
Yeah, kinda been all over

179
00:18:27,197 --> 00:18:30,076
Good to have you back here

180
00:18:30,076 --> 00:18:32,958
Thanks, Darryl. You keep enforcing the peace

181
00:18:32,958 --> 00:18:34,877
It'll be a little harder now that you're here
but I'll do what I can

182
00:18:34,877 --> 00:18:37,758
No man, I'm just visiting

183
00:18:37,758 --> 00:18:41,703
Hey, I'll see you around
Don't be a stranger, alright

184
00:19:06,559 --> 00:19:08,480
Sorry about yesterday

185
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,440
I don't care

186
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:12,319
I was studying the bus description
And I got on the wrong bus

187
00:19:12,319 --> 00:19:13,280
I missed my stop

188
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:17,119
I don't care, Terry. I'm so glad to see you

189
00:19:17,119 --> 00:19:20,959
I'm glad to see you too, Sammy

190
00:19:20,959 --> 00:19:22,881
So you're coming from work

191
00:19:22,881 --> 00:19:26,720
No, it's Saturday

192
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:30,560
Yeah, no, it's just that you dressed so formally

193
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:36,395
Oh, no, you know, I thought I'd...
I thought it was special occasion. Which it is

194
00:19:37,281 --> 00:19:40,161
No, it's good, it's good
I thought I'd get dressed up too

195
00:19:40,161 --> 00:19:42,081
It's okay. You look fine

196
00:19:42,081 --> 00:19:44,961
Yeah, this is the haute cuisine of garments

197
00:19:44,961 --> 00:19:45,922
What?

198
00:19:45,922 --> 00:19:49,750
Nothing. Nothing. So how are you?

199
00:19:52,642 --> 00:19:55,523
We're fine, Terry

200
00:19:55,523 --> 00:19:57,442
So, how's Rudy?

201
00:19:57,442 --> 00:20:01,282
We're fine, Terry

202
00:20:01,282 --> 00:20:04,162
How are you?

203
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:06,083
Yeah...

204
00:20:06,083 --> 00:20:08,962
Where have you been lately, Terry?

205
00:20:08,962 --> 00:20:10,884
I know, I haven't been...

206
00:20:10,884 --> 00:20:12,802
I got a postcard from you, from Alaska

207
00:20:12,802 --> 00:20:14,724
Yeah, yeah I was up there for a little while

208
00:20:14,724 --> 00:20:16,643
That was in the fall, Terry

209
00:20:16,643 --> 00:20:17,602
Yeah I know, I've been out of touch

210
00:20:17,602 --> 00:20:19,524
I was a little worried

211
00:20:19,524 --> 00:20:20,484
I've been a lot of different places. I was down

212
00:20:20,484 --> 00:20:24,324
in Florida for a little while
I was doing some work

213
00:20:24,324 --> 00:20:28,154
in Orlando. I've been all over the place

214
00:20:29,125 --> 00:20:33,250
Well I just wish
you had just let me know you were okay

215
00:20:33,925 --> 00:20:37,754
Yeah, I just didn't realize it had been so long

216
00:20:39,685 --> 00:20:43,515
You staying in town for a little while

217
00:20:44,485 --> 00:20:47,365
Well I don't know

218
00:20:47,365 --> 00:20:51,205
I got all these things
I got to do back in Worcester

219
00:20:51,205 --> 00:20:52,165
Oh

220
00:20:52,165 --> 00:20:56,005
Yeah, so I'm probably not gonna
be able to stay more than a day or so

221
00:20:56,005 --> 00:20:57,926
Oh...

222
00:20:57,926 --> 00:21:01,755
I'm kind of trying to keep to a schedule of sorts

223
00:21:02,726 --> 00:21:04,646
Oh, that's alright

224
00:21:04,646 --> 00:21:09,711
It's a long story and I don't want
to trouble you with it right now

225
00:21:19,046 --> 00:21:21,928
Are you expecting someone?

226
00:21:21,928 --> 00:21:23,846
Who would I be expecting here?

227
00:21:23,846 --> 00:21:25,767
You just keep looking around, that's all

228
00:21:25,767 --> 00:21:31,132
No, I was just wondering if we could
get some more refreshments, that's all

229
00:21:40,168 --> 00:21:43,048
I actually got to confess to you, Sammy

230
00:21:43,048 --> 00:21:46,889
That's the reason
you may not have heard from me for while

231
00:21:46,889 --> 00:21:50,724
is I've been unable to write on the account
of that

232
00:21:57,450 --> 00:22:00,329
I was in jail for a little while

233
00:22:00,329 --> 00:22:02,250
You were what?

234
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:06,089
I sort of did a little time, I guess
down in Florida, it was just bullshit

235
00:22:06,089 --> 00:22:07,050
What?

236
00:22:07,050 --> 00:22:08,010
It was bullshit!

237
00:22:08,010 --> 00:22:08,969
What did you do?

238
00:22:08,969 --> 00:22:10,890
I didn't do anything! Maybe I was wronged?

239
00:22:10,890 --> 00:22:12,810
No! Could I please... Oh my god!

240
00:22:12,810 --> 00:22:14,730
Please let me tell you what happened

241
00:22:14,730 --> 00:22:15,690
What happened?

242
00:22:15,690 --> 00:22:17,611
I got into a fight in a bar in Florida
I was not the one who started it

243
00:22:17,611 --> 00:22:19,530
But they worked up all this bullshit against me...

244
00:22:19,530 --> 00:22:22,411
and they threw me in the pen for 3 months
I didn't write you because...

245
00:22:22,411 --> 00:22:24,330
I didn't want you to get all upset about it

246
00:22:24,330 --> 00:22:28,171
I thought, you would figure that
I was on the road for a while

247
00:22:28,171 --> 00:22:31,051
It was stupid, I'm sorry
I didn't mean to make you worry

248
00:22:31,051 --> 00:22:32,971
But you know what. I can't run around
doing stuff for not doing stuff

249
00:22:32,971 --> 00:22:35,852
because it'll make you worry

250
00:22:35,852 --> 00:22:37,771
Because I come back here

251
00:22:37,771 --> 00:22:39,692
and tell you my fuckin' traumas
and I get this wounded

252
00:22:39,692 --> 00:22:41,612
I've let you down, bullshit. Over and over again
It just cramps me

253
00:22:41,612 --> 00:22:44,492
I just wanna get out from under it

254
00:22:44,492 --> 00:22:46,412
And now I'm back in this fucking hole
explaining myself to you again!

255
00:22:46,412 --> 00:22:48,332
Please stop cursing at me

256
00:22:48,332 --> 00:22:50,252
I mean, I realize I'm in no position
to basically say anything

257
00:22:50,252 --> 00:22:53,133
but it's not like I'm down there
in some redneck bar in Florida

258
00:22:53,133 --> 00:22:55,052
having an argument with some stripper's
boyfriend

259
00:22:55,052 --> 00:22:56,972
and I suddenly say to myself, hey
this would be

260
00:22:56,972 --> 00:22:58,894
a good time to really stick it to Sammy

261
00:22:58,894 --> 00:23:00,812
and get myself locked up for a few months

262
00:23:00,812 --> 00:23:04,653
You don't write me for 6 months
I don't know where you are

263
00:23:04,653 --> 00:23:06,572
I don't know if you're alive or dead

264
00:23:06,572 --> 00:23:08,494
Then you show up out of nowhere

265
00:23:08,494 --> 00:23:09,453
and you tell me you were in jail!

266
00:23:09,453 --> 00:23:12,335
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, Sammy

267
00:23:12,335 --> 00:23:16,163
I'm really sorry

268
00:23:26,735 --> 00:23:28,655
Sammy...

269
00:23:28,655 --> 00:23:30,573
What?

270
00:23:30,573 --> 00:23:33,455
I'm in the midst of a slight predicament

271
00:23:33,455 --> 00:23:34,415
What do you need, money?

272
00:23:34,415 --> 00:23:38,244
Um, yeah. I'm broke

273
00:23:39,215 --> 00:23:41,136
I gotta get back to Worcester tomorrow

274
00:23:41,136 --> 00:23:44,015
I got this girl there
and she's kind of in a bad situation

275
00:23:44,015 --> 00:23:47,845
So... I just need to borrow some money

276
00:23:48,815 --> 00:23:52,645
Whatever you can spare
I'll pay you back, man

277
00:23:54,577 --> 00:23:58,405
I'll pay you back

278
00:24:00,337 --> 00:24:03,216
I just...

279
00:24:03,216 --> 00:24:06,097
I really wish mom was here

280
00:24:06,097 --> 00:24:07,056
So do I, man

281
00:24:07,056 --> 00:24:09,938
No one knows what to do with you

282
00:24:09,938 --> 00:24:12,816
I know how they feel, man

283
00:24:12,816 --> 00:24:16,657
Terry, can I ask you a question?

284
00:24:16,657 --> 00:24:18,578
Sure

285
00:24:18,578 --> 00:24:22,406
I mean, do you ever go to church anymore?

286
00:24:24,338 --> 00:24:27,217
Sammy can we not talk about that shit?

287
00:24:27,217 --> 00:24:28,178
Do you?

288
00:24:28,178 --> 00:24:30,099
No, Sammy. I don't

289
00:24:30,099 --> 00:24:31,057
Can you tell me why not?

290
00:24:31,057 --> 00:24:33,938
Yeah, because I think it's ridiculous

291
00:24:33,938 --> 00:24:35,858
Well, can you tell me without denigrating it?

292
00:24:35,858 --> 00:24:38,738
It's primitive, okay, it's a fairy tale

293
00:24:38,738 --> 00:24:40,658
Well have you ever considered maybe that's

294
00:24:40,658 --> 00:24:42,579
what's making things so difficult for you?

295
00:24:42,579 --> 00:24:43,538
No

296
00:24:43,538 --> 00:24:44,499
That you've lost hold...

297
00:24:44,499 --> 00:24:47,379
not just your religious feeling
but lost hold of any kind of anchor

298
00:24:47,379 --> 00:24:49,299
Any kind of trust in anything

299
00:24:49,299 --> 00:24:53,139
No wonder you drift around so much
I mean...

300
00:24:53,139 --> 00:24:56,019
what's to stop you. How would you ever know
if you ever found the right thing

301
00:24:56,019 --> 00:25:01,014
I'm not looking for anything, man
I'm just trying to get on with it

302
00:25:03,700 --> 00:25:07,529
Here we go

303
00:25:10,421 --> 00:25:14,249
Thank you

304
00:25:44,022 --> 00:25:47,853
Thanks, Sammy
I'm really going to pay you back

305
00:26:00,343 --> 00:26:02,263
Where we going?

306
00:26:02,263 --> 00:26:06,094
Pick up Rudy

307
00:26:07,064 --> 00:26:08,983
Well, do you even want me to visit now?

308
00:26:08,983 --> 00:26:10,905
Because I can catch the bus at five o'clock
if that's what you want

309
00:26:10,905 --> 00:26:13,783
Of course I want you to visit, you idiot!

310
00:26:13,783 --> 00:26:15,705
I've been looking forward
to seeing you more than anything

311
00:26:15,705 --> 00:26:17,624
I've told everybody I know that
you were coming home

312
00:26:17,624 --> 00:26:20,505
I cleaned the whole fucking house
so it would look nice for you

313
00:26:20,505 --> 00:26:22,424
I thought you'd stay at least a few days...

314
00:26:22,424 --> 00:26:24,344
I had no idea that you were just broke again!

315
00:26:24,344 --> 00:26:28,174
I just wish you'd send me an invoice!

316
00:26:50,266 --> 00:26:53,146
Hi, is that, is that Malcom? Hi...

317
00:26:53,146 --> 00:26:56,986
this is Terry Prescott

318
00:26:56,986 --> 00:26:58,907
I've been trying to get a hold of Sheila...

319
00:26:58,907 --> 00:27:01,786
and the phone isn't picking up

320
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:05,627
And I was wondering if...

321
00:27:05,627 --> 00:27:09,457
She what?

322
00:27:13,308 --> 00:27:17,137
Well is she alright?

323
00:27:18,108 --> 00:27:21,937
Can I talk to her, please?

324
00:27:23,868 --> 00:27:27,698
Okay, could you please give her a message

325
00:27:28,668 --> 00:27:32,498
And tell that I...

326
00:27:40,189 --> 00:27:44,028
That girl I'm with tried to kill herself

327
00:27:44,028 --> 00:27:44,989
What?

328
00:27:44,989 --> 00:27:48,819
She tired to kill herself

329
00:28:01,311 --> 00:28:03,230
You have everything you need?

330
00:28:03,230 --> 00:28:07,060
I think so

331
00:28:15,711 --> 00:28:18,592
What are you going to do?

332
00:28:18,592 --> 00:28:22,421
I don't know. Send her the money I guess

333
00:28:25,312 --> 00:28:29,151
Maybe you should stay home for a while

334
00:28:29,151 --> 00:28:32,981
Yeah, maybe a good idea

335
00:28:56,993 --> 00:28:59,874
This 15 year old says
she's sick of her brother trying to control her

336
00:28:59,874 --> 00:29:05,654
Dropped out of school, she's doing drugs
says there's nothing he can do about it

337
00:29:23,876 --> 00:29:26,754
I'm going to bed

338
00:29:26,754 --> 00:29:28,676
You have everything you need?

339
00:29:28,676 --> 00:29:32,504
Ahh, yeah, thanks

340
00:29:33,476 --> 00:29:35,395
Goodnight

341
00:29:35,395 --> 00:29:38,277
Goodnight

342
00:29:38,277 --> 00:29:42,107
Terry, I'm really glad you're home

343
00:29:44,996 --> 00:29:48,826
Yeah me too, Sammy

344
00:29:57,477 --> 00:30:01,317
So we'll drop Rudy off at the bus, then all
you have to do is drop me off at the bank...

345
00:30:01,317 --> 00:30:05,157
and then pick Rudy up at 3:30

346
00:30:05,157 --> 00:30:08,997
and drive him over to Carol's house
And that's it, she lives on Harvey Lane

347
00:30:08,997 --> 00:30:11,878
Okay

348
00:30:11,878 --> 00:30:14,757
Rudy knows where she lives

349
00:30:14,757 --> 00:30:18,587
Okay

350
00:30:21,478 --> 00:30:24,358
God, Mabel, don't those colors hurt your eyes?

351
00:30:24,358 --> 00:30:28,198
Oh no, keeps me fresh

352
00:30:28,198 --> 00:30:31,079
Yeah?

353
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:33,959
Hi Sammy, what can I do for ya'?

354
00:30:33,959 --> 00:30:37,999
Umm, Brian, did you want us
to hand these time sheets...

355
00:30:38,760 --> 00:30:42,599
in at the end of the day or
at the end of the week?

356
00:30:42,599 --> 00:30:44,520
Oh, yeah. The end of the day will be fine

357
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:48,360
Just seems like an awful lot of extra paperwork

358
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:52,189
I like paperwork

359
00:31:20,042 --> 00:31:21,003
You showed up

360
00:31:21,003 --> 00:31:24,831
Looks that way

361
00:31:31,563 --> 00:31:32,522
Put on your seatbelt

362
00:31:32,522 --> 00:31:34,442
It pushes on my neck

363
00:31:34,442 --> 00:31:35,403
What?

364
00:31:35,403 --> 00:31:38,283
It pushes on my neck, it's uncomfortable

365
00:31:38,283 --> 00:31:41,163
Well, when somebody slams into us
and you go sailin' through the windshield

366
00:31:41,163 --> 00:31:45,603
that's liable to be uncomfortable too
Now put on your seatbelt

367
00:31:50,764 --> 00:31:52,683
Mom's parents died in a car accident

368
00:31:52,683 --> 00:31:54,604
Yeah, I know. They were my parents too

369
00:31:54,604 --> 00:31:55,564
They are?

370
00:31:55,564 --> 00:31:58,444
Yeah, your mom's my sister

371
00:31:58,444 --> 00:31:59,404
Yeah, I know

372
00:31:59,404 --> 00:32:01,324
So that means we have the same parents

373
00:32:01,324 --> 00:32:03,245
Oh yeah

374
00:32:03,245 --> 00:32:07,074
Oh yeah

375
00:32:09,964 --> 00:32:10,924
Umm, Carol just called

376
00:32:10,924 --> 00:32:14,765
She said Terry and Rudy
never showed up at her house

377
00:32:14,765 --> 00:32:17,646
You've got to be kidding

378
00:32:17,646 --> 00:32:21,485
It's supposed to filed by number
the account number, not alphabetically

379
00:32:21,485 --> 00:32:25,314
Sammy? Sammy!

380
00:32:52,207 --> 00:32:56,047
Hey. Look, if you hold it further down, you're

381
00:32:56,047 --> 00:32:57,966
gonna get a lot more power
You should be able

382
00:32:57,966 --> 00:32:59,887
to hit that nail in with two or three hits. Look

383
00:32:59,887 --> 00:33:03,715
See? Go ahead, try it

384
00:33:06,607 --> 00:33:08,527
That's not the way I hold it

385
00:33:08,527 --> 00:33:10,447
Well they way you hold it, is wrong

386
00:33:10,447 --> 00:33:12,367
Why can't I just hold it my own way

387
00:33:12,367 --> 00:33:16,196
You can...

388
00:33:53,650 --> 00:33:57,480
Alright, good, that's good

389
00:33:58,450 --> 00:34:02,280
Sammy, please see me, ASAP!!! Brian

390
00:34:07,091 --> 00:34:09,971
Brian, did you want to see me?

391
00:34:09,971 --> 00:34:12,851
Yeah, I was kinda wondering
what happened to you today

392
00:34:12,851 --> 00:34:16,691
Didn't Mabel tell you
I had a false alarm about my son

393
00:34:16,691 --> 00:34:18,611
Yeah well I kind of thought
you were gonna work that out?

394
00:34:18,611 --> 00:34:20,531
I did work it out. More or less

395
00:34:20,531 --> 00:34:22,452
Then what are you doing
leaving here in the middle of the day

396
00:34:22,452 --> 00:34:25,331
Without so much
as a word of explanation to me, Sammy

397
00:34:25,331 --> 00:34:26,292
Brian, don't yell at me...

398
00:34:26,292 --> 00:34:30,131
I'm not yelling at you
I'm just... getting a little frustrated here

399
00:34:30,131 --> 00:34:31,093
Well...

400
00:34:31,093 --> 00:34:34,922
Sorry, would you close the door, please

401
00:34:35,892 --> 00:34:39,734
And Eddie Dwyer lives in Buffalo, with his wife
and two kids, if you can believe it

402
00:34:39,734 --> 00:34:40,692
That's depressing

403
00:34:40,692 --> 00:34:41,653
Why?

404
00:34:41,653 --> 00:34:44,533
I just never expected him the marrying type

405
00:34:44,533 --> 00:34:46,452
Who are you talking about?

406
00:34:46,452 --> 00:34:48,374
Some wild kids we use to know

407
00:34:48,374 --> 00:34:49,333
Were you a wild kid?

408
00:34:49,333 --> 00:34:50,294
Not as wild as your mom

409
00:34:50,294 --> 00:34:51,253
Yeah, right

410
00:34:51,253 --> 00:34:52,215
You don't believe me? No

411
00:34:52,215 --> 00:34:53,173
Ask her

412
00:34:53,173 --> 00:34:57,004
Mom, were you?

413
00:34:57,974 --> 00:35:01,804
No comment

414
00:35:50,777 --> 00:35:53,657
What are you doing?

415
00:35:53,657 --> 00:35:57,496
Oh... Just reading some of your compositions

416
00:35:57,496 --> 00:35:58,458
Why are you smoking?

417
00:35:58,458 --> 00:36:01,337
Uhh, because it's bad. Don't ever do it

418
00:36:01,337 --> 00:36:05,167
I won't

419
00:36:06,137 --> 00:36:09,018
You know this used to be my room?

420
00:36:09,018 --> 00:36:11,897
Yeah

421
00:36:11,897 --> 00:36:14,778
Do you want it back?

422
00:36:14,778 --> 00:36:18,608
No

423
00:36:19,578 --> 00:36:22,460
Did you fight in Vietnam?

424
00:36:22,460 --> 00:36:24,379
No. I wasn't even born yet

425
00:36:24,379 --> 00:36:25,338
Were you ever in the Army?

426
00:36:25,338 --> 00:36:27,259
No

427
00:36:27,259 --> 00:36:28,219
My father was in the Army

428
00:36:28,219 --> 00:36:29,178
I know

429
00:36:29,178 --> 00:36:32,059
Unfortunately he didn't fight in Vietnam either

430
00:36:32,059 --> 00:36:34,938
Were you friends with him?

431
00:36:34,938 --> 00:36:39,213
Not really, I mean
we had some friends in common I guess...

432
00:36:39,740 --> 00:36:41,661
I didn't like him very much

433
00:36:41,661 --> 00:36:43,580
Why not?

434
00:36:43,580 --> 00:36:45,500
Well... He wasn't very likeable

435
00:36:45,500 --> 00:36:47,419
Why do you say that?

436
00:36:47,419 --> 00:36:51,529
I don't know
he was always better than you at everything

437
00:36:52,221 --> 00:36:56,061
Like if you were all playing basketball or
something, everybody's have like a friendly game

438
00:36:56,061 --> 00:36:59,900
he was ready to kill somebody
if his team didn't win

439
00:36:59,900 --> 00:37:01,821
Or if you told a joke or a story

440
00:37:01,821 --> 00:37:03,741
he always had to tell a better one

441
00:37:03,741 --> 00:37:05,661
Kinda gets annoying after awhile

442
00:37:05,661 --> 00:37:08,541
Plus it was pretty scummy
how he split on you and your mom

443
00:37:08,541 --> 00:37:10,462
He was a prick. Probably still a prick

444
00:37:10,462 --> 00:37:14,432
Fortunately for you though
your mom is like the greatest

445
00:37:15,262 --> 00:37:19,091
So you had some bad luck
and some good luck

446
00:37:24,862 --> 00:37:26,783
You mind if I ask you a personal question?

447
00:37:26,783 --> 00:37:28,703
I don't know

448
00:37:28,703 --> 00:37:32,532
Do you like it here? I mean, in Scotsville

449
00:37:33,502 --> 00:37:34,463
Yeah

450
00:37:34,463 --> 00:37:37,344
Why?

451
00:37:37,344 --> 00:37:38,302
I don't know...

452
00:37:38,302 --> 00:37:41,182
My friends are here, I like the scenery
I don't know

453
00:37:41,182 --> 00:37:45,023
I know... It's so... There's nothing to do here

454
00:37:45,023 --> 00:37:45,985
Yes there is

455
00:37:45,985 --> 00:37:48,863
No there isn't man, it's narrow. It's dull

456
00:37:48,863 --> 00:37:51,744
It's a dull
narrow town full of dull narrow people

457
00:37:51,744 --> 00:37:55,584
who don't know anything except
what things are like right around here

458
00:37:55,584 --> 00:37:58,464
They have no perspective whatsoever
No scope

459
00:37:58,464 --> 00:38:01,344
They might as well be living in the
19th century...

460
00:38:01,344 --> 00:38:04,224
because they have no idea of
what's going on...

461
00:38:04,224 --> 00:38:07,104
and if you try to tell 'em that
they wanna fuckin' kill you

462
00:38:07,104 --> 00:38:09,985
What are you talking about?

463
00:38:09,985 --> 00:38:13,815
I have no idea

464
00:38:14,785 --> 00:38:18,614
you're a good kid

465
00:38:20,545 --> 00:38:24,376
Sammy, please see me... Brian

466
00:38:31,106 --> 00:38:33,028
Yeah, this doesn't apply to you
Sammy, but...

467
00:38:33,028 --> 00:38:36,866
I've noticed that some of the employees
are setting their PC monitors...

468
00:38:36,866 --> 00:38:39,747
to all kinds of crazy colors
Purple, polks dots...

469
00:38:39,747 --> 00:38:42,627
what have you
And it's no big deal, but really...

470
00:38:42,627 --> 00:38:45,506
this is a bank. You know?
It's really not appropriate

471
00:38:45,506 --> 00:38:48,388
So I'm just asking that
people use the more quote unquote...

472
00:38:48,388 --> 00:38:52,229
normal range of colors in the future

473
00:38:52,229 --> 00:38:55,106
Like I said, this doesn't really apply to you

474
00:38:55,106 --> 00:38:58,938
No. My computer palette's pretty conservative

475
00:39:36,389 --> 00:39:37,350
Bob Steegerson

476
00:39:37,350 --> 00:39:41,190
What are you wearing?

477
00:39:41,190 --> 00:39:45,020
Mom?

478
00:39:47,910 --> 00:39:48,871
What's up?

479
00:39:48,871 --> 00:39:53,876
Do you know you have an enormous leak
coming from the upstairs hallway?

480
00:39:55,590 --> 00:39:59,421
Yeah, I did

481
00:40:00,390 --> 00:40:04,221
You guys sure you're going to be okay?

482
00:40:05,192 --> 00:40:06,150
Yes. Yes

483
00:40:06,150 --> 00:40:07,111
What is happening here?

484
00:40:07,111 --> 00:40:10,951
It's just the problem is, the pipe is corroded
the whole length of the hall

485
00:40:10,951 --> 00:40:13,833
So every time I put in a new piece
it starts leaking further down

486
00:40:13,833 --> 00:40:14,792
Why don't I just call the plumber?

487
00:40:14,792 --> 00:40:18,632
Why? He's not gonna do anything
different than what I'm doing

488
00:40:18,632 --> 00:40:19,592
Yeah, we're making it worse

489
00:40:19,592 --> 00:40:23,422
No we're not. Shut up...

490
00:40:30,152 --> 00:40:33,993
Thanks. Thank you

491
00:40:33,993 --> 00:40:35,913
So call if there's any problems

492
00:40:35,913 --> 00:40:38,793
and if I'm not there. I'm either
on my way back home or on my way

493
00:40:38,793 --> 00:40:39,755
Okay

494
00:40:39,755 --> 00:40:40,714
Nice to meet you, Bob

495
00:40:40,714 --> 00:40:43,594
You too

496
00:40:43,594 --> 00:40:46,473
So lights out at ten
and don't spend the whole night watching TV

497
00:40:46,473 --> 00:40:48,394
What's your idea of the whole night?

498
00:40:48,394 --> 00:40:52,225
2 hours, tops

499
00:40:59,915 --> 00:41:05,915
This kid is a sure bet to lead the way
for the next generation of California Surfers

500
00:41:07,595 --> 00:41:09,516
What's your feeling about Bob?

501
00:41:09,516 --> 00:41:13,355
I don't really know him that well

502
00:41:13,355 --> 00:41:15,275
I have bad news for you

503
00:41:15,275 --> 00:41:19,115
No...

504
00:41:19,115 --> 00:41:21,996
Great. What are we supposed to do now?

505
00:41:21,996 --> 00:41:23,916
Do you know how to play pool?

506
00:41:23,916 --> 00:41:27,746
I've played it

507
00:41:35,438 --> 00:41:37,357
I don't think they let kids in here. What?

508
00:41:37,357 --> 00:41:39,277
I don't think they let kids in here

509
00:41:39,277 --> 00:41:43,116
Well, we're not allowed to watch any more TV
so it's this or nothing

510
00:41:43,116 --> 00:41:45,037
But if we get into trouble
let me do the talking. Okay?

511
00:41:45,037 --> 00:41:48,866
Okay

512
00:41:51,758 --> 00:41:55,598
I got a hundred bucks here says
me and my nephew can beat anybody in here

513
00:41:55,598 --> 00:42:01,118
Only we gotta get the next game
because he's gotta be in bed by 10 o'clock

514
00:42:03,278 --> 00:42:07,118
Just hit it nice and soft, nice and soft

515
00:42:07,118 --> 00:42:10,948
One, two, three

516
00:42:12,877 --> 00:42:14,799
Sorry

517
00:42:14,799 --> 00:42:18,630
God damn it, Rudy
I thought you said you could play

518
00:42:32,079 --> 00:42:35,909
Boys, it's all over but the cryin'

519
00:42:58,001 --> 00:43:00,883
Bob, are you serious?

520
00:43:00,883 --> 00:43:02,802
Yeah

521
00:43:02,802 --> 00:43:06,632
I don't know what to say...

522
00:43:07,603 --> 00:43:11,433
Look... I mean... I know that umm...

523
00:43:13,361 --> 00:43:17,192
I haven't been the most...
decisive guy in the past

524
00:43:22,003 --> 00:43:25,832
But, I don't know. I am tired of fooling around

525
00:43:26,804 --> 00:43:30,634
And I love you

526
00:43:31,603 --> 00:43:35,434
