That wasn't him. I heard him tell the cops

1043
01:25:57,222 --> 01:26:01,062
No, Rudy, that was him

1044
01:26:01,062 --> 01:26:02,982
I wish it wasn't, but it was

1045
01:26:02,982 --> 01:26:04,901
No it wasn't

1046
01:26:04,901 --> 01:26:08,732
Yes, Rudy it was

1047
01:26:11,622 --> 01:26:15,552
Your father's name is Rudy Kolinsky
He lives in Auburn

1048
01:26:38,503 --> 01:26:42,334
Would you turn it off, please?

1049
01:26:45,224 --> 01:26:47,144
You don't have to say anything, Sammy

1050
01:26:47,144 --> 01:26:50,975
I want you to leave

1051
01:26:51,944 --> 01:26:54,824
What do you mean?

1052
01:26:54,824 --> 01:26:58,664
I mean, I don't think you should live here

1053
01:26:58,664 --> 01:27:01,546
I don't think you know how to behave
around an eight year old...

1054
01:27:01,546 --> 01:27:03,465
and I don't know how to make you stop

1055
01:27:03,465 --> 01:27:08,295
So I don't think you should live here
I don't know what else say

1056
01:27:09,226 --> 01:27:10,186
I don't know how to behave
around an eight year old...

1057
01:27:10,186 --> 01:27:11,145
That's right

1058
01:27:11,145 --> 01:27:13,066
I think you don't know how to behave
around an eight year old

1059
01:27:13,066 --> 01:27:16,905
Are you out of your mind?

1060
01:27:16,905 --> 01:27:18,826
Now you just listen to me

1061
01:27:18,826 --> 01:27:20,746
I may not be the greatest mother in the world

1062
01:27:20,746 --> 01:27:22,667
But I'm doing the best I know how

1063
01:27:22,667 --> 01:27:24,586
And he doesn't need you to rub his face in shit...

1064
01:27:24,586 --> 01:27:26,508
because you think it's good for him!

1065
01:27:26,508 --> 01:27:29,386
He's going to find out the world is a
horrible place

1066
01:27:29,386 --> 01:27:34,681
and that people suck soon enough
and without any help from you. Believe me!

1067
01:27:38,027 --> 01:27:41,857
I think you should get your own place

1068
01:27:42,827 --> 01:27:47,157
I thought, maybe...
I'd be happy to help you out financially

1069
01:27:47,627 --> 01:27:50,247
What do you mean, get my own place?

1070
01:27:51,468 --> 01:27:52,428
Yes. Yes

1071
01:27:52,428 --> 01:27:56,263
Why would I do that?
Why don't I just leave, period

1072
01:28:00,108 --> 01:28:03,940
If that's what you want to do, that's fine

1073
01:28:04,908 --> 01:28:09,778
But that's not what I'm saying
You are an important person to Rudy

1074
01:28:11,628 --> 01:28:14,510
And you are the most important person to me

1075
01:28:14,510 --> 01:28:17,389
But I'm saying I can't take anymore of this

1076
01:28:17,389 --> 01:28:19,311
Well...

1077
01:28:19,311 --> 01:28:23,151
And I thought you could sell
your half of the house to me

1078
01:28:23,151 --> 01:28:26,029
And then I could pay you back a certain
amount, whatever it is...

1079
01:28:26,029 --> 01:28:26,990
over a certain period of time

1080
01:28:26,990 --> 01:28:30,819
No, you know what, I'll just go

1081
01:28:34,670 --> 01:28:38,501
Well, that's not what I'm saying

1082
01:28:43,311 --> 01:28:45,230
Where you gonna go?

1083
01:28:45,230 --> 01:28:48,112
I don't know, I just want out of this town

1084
01:28:48,112 --> 01:28:50,030
And if you've got any sense
when you're older you'll leave too

1085
01:28:50,030 --> 01:28:52,912
You know your mom's going to stay
in this town for the rest of her life

1086
01:28:52,912 --> 01:28:55,791
You wanna know why?
Because she thinks she has to

1087
01:28:55,791 --> 01:28:58,671
She thinks there's all these things she has to do

1088
01:28:58,671 --> 01:28:59,631
I'll tell you one thing about your mom

1089
01:28:59,631 --> 01:29:02,512
She's a bigger fuck up than I ever was

1090
01:29:02,512 --> 01:29:04,431
I know I messed up, okay

1091
01:29:04,431 --> 01:29:07,312
You think I enjoy getting thrown in jail?

1092
01:29:07,312 --> 01:29:12,111
Because I wanted you to face that prick
your Dad, like a little man

1093
01:29:12,112 --> 01:29:14,033
And show you what kind of guy he is?
I got carried away, I know...

1094
01:29:14,033 --> 01:29:16,912
I lost my temper, just a little bit...

1095
01:29:16,912 --> 01:29:22,512
Which is not the end of the world either
by the way, just for future reference

1096
01:29:22,673 --> 01:29:24,593
And now she's throwing me out of
my own home

1097
01:29:24,593 --> 01:29:28,424
because, I fucked up a little bit

1098
01:29:31,314 --> 01:29:34,194
Which I totally admit...

1099
01:29:34,194 --> 01:29:36,114
I was like, totally ready to admit that

1100
01:29:36,114 --> 01:29:39,944
I could go with you

1101
01:29:43,795 --> 01:29:48,320
Well thanks man, but I ahh...
I can't really take care of you

1102
01:29:57,236 --> 01:29:58,195
Is that for you?

1103
01:29:58,195 --> 01:30:02,036
Yeah, I'm just gonna stay at Ray's until I leave

1104
01:30:02,036 --> 01:30:03,956
Well, you don't have to do that

1105
01:30:03,956 --> 01:30:05,876
Yeah, well, that's what I wanna do

1106
01:30:05,876 --> 01:30:08,756
Well... Are you gonna come back
and say goodbye?

1107
01:30:08,756 --> 01:30:12,586
No, I'm just gonna take off, I'll see ya'

1108
01:30:26,037 --> 01:30:27,958
Look, I know you're upset about
Uncle Terry leaving

1109
01:30:27,958 --> 01:30:28,916
and so am I

1110
01:30:28,916 --> 01:30:30,838
But he's not in control of himself

1111
01:30:30,838 --> 01:30:33,717
And I don't want him hurting your feelings
anymore or mine

1112
01:30:33,717 --> 01:30:36,597
And you may not like it but that's
how it's going to be. Okay?

1113
01:30:36,597 --> 01:30:38,517
I don't care

1114
01:30:38,517 --> 01:30:42,357
You don't care? I don't care either

1115
01:30:42,357 --> 01:30:44,279
Well I'm sorry you're having all this trouble

1116
01:30:44,279 --> 01:30:45,238
Thank you

1117
01:30:45,238 --> 01:30:47,157
You made a pretty good speech to me
the other day about people...

1118
01:30:47,157 --> 01:30:49,079
sticking to their commitments. Yeah

1119
01:30:49,079 --> 01:30:53,299
Well you made a commitment Sammy
to this bank, to this job

1120
01:30:53,878 --> 01:30:54,838
I know I did

1121
01:30:54,838 --> 01:30:55,798
And to work things out with this tough new

1122
01:30:55,798 --> 01:30:58,679
son of a bitch boss of yours

1123
01:30:58,679 --> 01:31:01,560
How whatever may have passed
between us after hours...

1124
01:31:01,560 --> 01:31:04,439
doesn't mean you can walk away
from that commitment

1125
01:31:04,439 --> 01:31:08,279
Yeah, even if you have a
legitimate family emergency

1126
01:31:08,279 --> 01:31:10,200
I'm really sorry I didn't call in...

1127
01:31:10,200 --> 01:31:12,120
That is why I think
in the calm cold light of day...

1128
01:31:12,120 --> 01:31:15,960
that you and I have to both think real hard...

1129
01:31:15,960 --> 01:31:21,130
about whether you really want to continue
on here at Outpost Bankers Trust

1130
01:31:22,681 --> 01:31:23,640
You've got to be kidding

1131
01:31:23,640 --> 01:31:26,522
You're not happy, I'm not happy
and it's not good for you...

1132
01:31:26,522 --> 01:31:30,360
and it's sure as heck not good for the bank

1133
01:31:30,360 --> 01:31:32,282
You know, you're the worst manager
we've ever had

1134
01:31:32,282 --> 01:31:33,240
Come on, Sammy...

1135
01:31:33,240 --> 01:31:35,161
By far, the worst

1136
01:31:35,161 --> 01:31:36,122
I don't want to trade insults with you

1137
01:31:36,122 --> 01:31:39,000
Well I don't want to be fired
Brian. I've been here for 7 years

1138
01:31:39,000 --> 01:31:41,881
And if I were you
I'd be a little nervous about firing an employee...

1139
01:31:41,881 --> 01:31:45,712
I just had an affair with. Okay

1140
01:31:46,682 --> 01:31:47,641
Don't threaten me...

1141
01:31:47,641 --> 01:31:48,601
I'm not threatening you

1142
01:31:48,601 --> 01:31:50,522
I'm not threatening you

1143
01:31:50,522 --> 01:31:53,401
I just think it's an area we should explore

1144
01:31:53,401 --> 01:31:57,243
You explore it, I'm going back to work

1145
01:31:57,243 --> 01:32:00,122
Oh, and I have to pick up Rudy today

1146
01:32:00,122 --> 01:32:02,043
because there's no one else who can do it
I'll find someone else when I have time

1147
01:32:02,043 --> 01:32:03,963
Yeah fine

1148
01:32:03,963 --> 01:32:07,792
Why don't you just take over the whole bank

1149
01:32:27,966 --> 01:32:30,844
Well, I called Uncle Terry
where he said he'd be staying...

1150
01:32:30,844 --> 01:32:35,509
and there was no answer
So I don't know if he's still in town

1151
01:32:42,365 --> 01:32:46,195
Rudy, you're not speaking to me?

1152
01:32:51,966 --> 01:32:55,805
Well, I'm sorry you're mad at me
but I only did what I had to do

1153
01:32:55,805 --> 01:33:00,525
I just hope you don't stay mad at me
for the rest of your life

1154
01:33:12,126 --> 01:33:13,086
Rudy, that's enough

1155
01:33:13,086 --> 01:33:15,967
Rudy!

1156
01:33:15,967 --> 01:33:18,848
Now you got to cut this out!

1157
01:33:18,848 --> 01:33:19,806
What did I do?

1158
01:33:19,806 --> 01:33:22,688
You don't know what you're talking about!
There was nothing else I could do!

1159
01:33:22,688 --> 01:33:24,606
I don't know how to explain it to you
any better than that, but...

1160
01:33:24,606 --> 01:33:28,448
you cannot go on this way
because you don't know anything about it...

1161
01:33:28,448 --> 01:33:29,407
and you don't know what you're doing!

1162
01:33:29,407 --> 01:33:30,367
Okay, I'm sorry!

1163
01:33:30,367 --> 01:33:33,248
I don't want you to be sorry
I want you to stop it!

1164
01:33:33,248 --> 01:33:37,077
I'm stopping

1165
01:33:38,048 --> 01:33:41,877
See, I'm stopping. I'm stopping

1166
01:35:38,054 --> 01:35:41,886
Ray's house

1167
01:35:43,815 --> 01:35:45,736
I didn't know if you'd left yet

1168
01:35:45,736 --> 01:35:48,615
No, I'm leaving tomorrow

1169
01:35:48,615 --> 01:35:51,496
What time?

1170
01:35:51,496 --> 01:35:53,416
Umm, bus leaves at 9

1171
01:35:53,416 --> 01:35:57,245
Well, I'd really like to see you before you go

1172
01:35:59,176 --> 01:36:03,016
I mean, can I give you a lift
do you want to have breakfast or anything

1173
01:36:03,016 --> 01:36:06,856
I think Rudy, would really like to say goodbye

1174
01:36:06,856 --> 01:36:08,776
Yeah, I don't know, I mean...

1175
01:36:08,776 --> 01:36:11,657
Terry, you can't just leave like this

1176
01:36:11,657 --> 01:36:15,486
Alright, alright, I'll come by tomorrow morning

1177
01:36:16,457 --> 01:36:20,297
Alright, but just...

1178
01:36:20,297 --> 01:36:24,138
we have to be out of the house by 8 o'clock
so I don't want to tell Rudy you're coming...

1179
01:36:24,138 --> 01:36:26,057
unless you think you can make it

1180
01:36:26,057 --> 01:36:27,019
no... I'll be there

1181
01:36:27,019 --> 01:36:28,938
Alright

1182
01:36:28,938 --> 01:36:32,768
Alright

1183
01:36:48,140 --> 01:36:51,968
You better get your sneakers on

1184
01:37:07,340 --> 01:37:09,261
Sweetie, I'm sorry, but we have to go

1185
01:37:09,261 --> 01:37:13,089
Why can't I miss school one day?

1186
01:37:20,780 --> 01:37:23,662
Hey, how's it going, man

1187
01:37:23,662 --> 01:37:27,491
Sorry I'm late

1188
01:37:31,342 --> 01:37:34,221
So Rudy, if I write you a letter
will you write me back?

1189
01:37:34,221 --> 01:37:35,182
Yeah

1190
01:37:35,182 --> 01:37:39,021
That's gonna be pretty nice for you, because
I write a pretty Goddamn interesting letter

1191
01:37:39,021 --> 01:37:40,942
Yeah, we'll see

1192
01:37:40,942 --> 01:37:44,771
Well, alright, say goodbye

1193
01:37:54,382 --> 01:37:58,212
Bye

1194
01:38:18,385 --> 01:38:20,304
You need some cash for the bus?

1195
01:38:20,304 --> 01:38:24,554
No, I got a few bucks
aren't you gonna be late for work?

1196
01:38:27,025 --> 01:38:30,855
Oh, yeah... That's okay

1197
01:38:31,825 --> 01:38:35,666
Terry, I don't even know where you're going

1198
01:38:35,666 --> 01:38:39,541
Well, yeah... I don't really
have a concrete plan yet

1199
01:38:40,466 --> 01:38:42,385
I got to go back to Worcester and get my stuff

1200
01:38:42,385 --> 01:38:44,306
Oh, you're gonna try and see that girl?

1201
01:38:44,306 --> 01:38:46,225
Yeah, you know
I thought I'd try and show my face...

1202
01:38:46,225 --> 01:38:48,147
let her brother have a crack at me

1203
01:38:48,147 --> 01:38:49,108
What?

1204
01:38:49,108 --> 01:38:50,065
No...

1205
01:38:50,065 --> 01:38:51,985
I don't want anyone to have a crack at you

1206
01:38:51,985 --> 01:38:56,786
I'm just kidding. I just thought
I just thought I'd check up on her

1207
01:38:56,787 --> 01:38:59,666
And then after that, I don't know

1208
01:38:59,666 --> 01:39:01,588
I've been thinking about Alaska a lot

1209
01:39:01,588 --> 01:39:03,507
I still got a lot of friends out there

1210
01:39:03,507 --> 01:39:06,388
I don't really know

1211
01:39:06,388 --> 01:39:09,268
Anyway, I'll write you

1212
01:39:09,268 --> 01:39:12,147
You will?

1213
01:39:12,147 --> 01:39:15,978
Sure, Sammy. Of course I will, you know that

1214
01:39:18,869 --> 01:39:22,697
What is gonna happen to you?

1215
01:39:23,669 --> 01:39:27,497
Nothing too bad. But I gotta tell you, Sammy...

1216
01:39:29,428 --> 01:39:31,349
I know things didn't work out too well
this time...

1217
01:39:31,349 --> 01:39:35,189
but it's really good to know, wherever I am...

1218
01:39:35,189 --> 01:39:40,569
whatever stupid shit I'm doing
that you're back at my home, rooting for me

1219
01:39:41,909 --> 01:39:43,831
It's all going to be alright, Sammy

1220
01:39:43,831 --> 01:39:47,658
Comparatively, and I'll be back
around this way again

1221
01:39:49,590 --> 01:39:52,470
I just feel like I'm never going to see you again

1222
01:39:52,470 --> 01:39:55,350
Of course you will, you never have to
worry about that, ever

1223
01:39:55,350 --> 01:39:59,190
Don't go anywhere
until you know where you're going

1224
01:39:59,190 --> 01:40:03,030
I do, I do know where I'm going
I'm going back to Worcester

1225
01:40:03,030 --> 01:40:04,950
I'm going to try and see that girl

1226
01:40:04,950 --> 01:40:09,750
And then depending on what happens there
I'm going to see if there's work for me out west

1227
01:40:09,751 --> 01:40:12,631
And if there is, I'm going out there
this summer and make some money

1228
01:40:12,631 --> 01:40:15,511
And if there isn't, I'll figure something else out

1229
01:40:15,511 --> 01:40:17,431
Maybe I'll stay in the east. I don't know...

1230
01:40:17,431 --> 01:40:21,746
I really liked Alaska
It was really beautiful, and it just...

1231
01:40:24,151 --> 01:40:28,371
It made me feel good
And before things got so messed up...

1232
01:40:28,951 --> 01:40:32,791
I was doing pretty well out there

1233
01:40:32,791 --> 01:40:34,712
Seriously

1234
01:40:34,712 --> 01:40:38,837
But I couldn't stay here, Sammy
I don't wanna live here

1235
01:40:40,474 --> 01:40:42,392
But I'll keep in touch

1236
01:40:42,392 --> 01:40:45,273
And I will be back, because
I want to see you and I want to see Rudy

1237
01:40:45,273 --> 01:40:49,102
We'll have Christmas together, how's that?

1238
01:40:51,033 --> 01:40:53,913
We'll all have Christmas together

1239
01:40:53,913 --> 01:40:57,742
Come on, Sammy. You can trust me

1240
01:41:04,474 --> 01:41:08,306
Come on, Sammy, look at me... Look at me...

1241
01:41:13,115 --> 01:41:16,953
Sammy, remember when we were kids

1242
01:41:16,953 --> 01:41:18,876
Remember what we always
used to say to each other

1243
01:41:18,876 --> 01:41:20,794
Of course I do

1244
01:41:20,794 --> 01:41:24,625
Remember when we were kids

1245
01:41:29,435 --> 01:41:33,266
I'll really miss you
